## 2026-07-14 — Issue #1546 (projection-vocabulary ratchet)

The ratchet was substantially re-architected mid-review under maintainer direction (8
corrections). Most stage-1 deviations were RESOLVED and are NOT deficiencies:
- Conformance fixtures: now authored in the slice's consumed convention
  (`tests/structural.ttl` gmeow:StructuralAssertion invariants + a MUST-NOT counter-example),
  red/green-probed — not docs prose.
- Competency query: wired per convention (`queries/qc/`, registered as
  `ex:cqProjectionCeilingsHold` in `tests/competency.ttl`).
- Regenerate + generated `generated/governance/slice-quality-projection-{ceilings,vocabularies}.tsv`
  + `gmeow.gts` fold: produced (make regenerate run); the ratchet gate passes GREEN
  (`gmeow-dev slice-quality-gate` exit 0, 124 committed cells).

Recorded deviations (honest):
- WEAKER-THAN-PROPOSED RDFS COUNTED SET: `countKindStructuralAxiom` for `rdfs:` counts only
  `rdfs:subClassOf`/`rdfs:subPropertyOf` (the subsumption taxonomy), NOT the `rdfs:domain`/
  `rdfs:range` I originally proposed under "minimum useful structural set." Reason: counting
  property signatures made the projection-vocab schema's OWN new `rdfs:domain`/`range` (60
  lines) net-new debt that the grandfather gate correctly refused to grandfather (a
  self-referential bootstrap). Narrowing to the subsumption taxonomy is a faithful reading of
  "minimum useful structural set" and resolves the bootstrap; property signatures are RBox
  declarations, not migration debt. Domain/range are simply not guarded by this ratchet.
- OWL NOT GUARDED AT ALL (maintainer decision "definitely no OWL"): the permanent OWL/RDFS
  carve-out doctrine was removed, but only RDFS-subsumption is guarded; declarative OWL is left
  to the existing `reason-verify` gate.
- LARGE GRANDFATHERED SEED: the strict owner-boundary + rdfs + SHACL-obligation counting produce
  124 grandfathered ceiling cells (vs 33), including cross-slice external-reference debt (e.g.
  correspondence cells in non-owner core slices). This is intended debt, seeded at current
  measured and lower-only; migration ratchets it down.
- `projection-debt` REPORT CLI HOST: the live-measured debt report remains on
  `gmeow-dev slice-quality-projection-debt` (it needs a repo checkout to scan). The shippable
  `gmeow slice projection-ceilings` (landed) surfaces the COMMITMENTS view — the registry +
  124 committed ceilings from the bundle — but not the live measured/headroom, which stays on
  `gmeow-dev`. A shippable live-measured surface would require shipping a repo scan and is not
